# Third-party process-lifetime allocations made while Spring initializes its
# OpenGL driver. These frames are owned by the proprietary NVIDIA driver,
# outside Spring's ownership. Keep this intentionally narrow: an allocation
# whose stack reaches editor or engine code still fails LeakSanitizer.
leak:libnvidia-glcore.so

# NVIDIA registers with the session bus during driver initialization. The
# resulting libdbus allocations are owned by that process-lifetime setup and
# have no teardown API available to the engine.
leak:dbus_bus_register

# TODO(engine-leak): FreeType keeps its process-global font services/cache alive
# until process exit. Remove these rules when the engine owns and tears down
# that cache; this is unrelated to the Wasm implementation.
leak:tt_services
leak:ft_mem_alloc
leak:FT_New_Memory

# TODO(engine-leak): SDL's loopback-audio bookkeeping is allocated by the
# OpenAL sound thread and remains process-lifetime state after the engine's
# cleanup call. These rules are restricted to the two known Spring call sites
# that create/destroy that third-party state; remove them when that lifetime is
# fixed. This is unrelated to the Wasm implementation.
leak:CSound::OpenSdlDevice
leak:CSound::Cleanup
